# Build output. ~1400 crates and a 34 MB exe; everything in here is
# regenerated by `cargo build`, and `build.rs`'s rasterised logo.png and
# .ico land in OUT_DIR under it.
/target/

# The code knowledge graph. Regenerated in ~12 s by
# `graphify extract . --code-only --cargo` then `graphify cluster-only .`,
# so it is output, not source. (`.graphifyignore` keeps it out of its own
# input for the same reason.)
/graphify-out/

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This is a binary crate, and two
# of its pins are load-bearing: gpui-component is held at exactly =0.5.1
# (the last release on crates.io gpui 0.2.2), and the lock still carries
# cc 1.2.67. A resolver left to its own devices would undo both.

# Loose binaries, in case one is ever built outside target/.
*.exe
*.pdb
*.dll
*.so

# Editors and tools.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.rs.bk
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS litter.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# The app's own stores -- profiles.json, settings.json, session.json,
# known_hosts.json -- live in the platform data directory, not here, so
# they are out of reach by construction. These two lines are the guard for
# the one way they could arrive: a plugins_dir pointed inside the checkout,
# or a store copied in to look at. No secret is ever written to any of them
# (see store::SavedAuth), but a known_hosts pin and a host list are still
# nobody else's business.
# /plugins/
*.session.json
